.TH ag-migrate 1  "migrate 0.3.0-beta.2" 
.SH NAME
ag\-migrate \- Migrate every branch and tag from a full local Git clone or bundle into a new repository
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBag migrate\fR [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-repo\fR] [\fB\-\-as\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-lossy\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fB\-\-namespace\fR> <\fISOURCE\fR> <\fIDESTINATION\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Migrate every branch and tag from a full local Git clone or bundle into a new repository
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-repo\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Operate on the repository at this path (default: discovered from the current directory)
.TP
\fB\-\-namespace\fR \fI<NAMESPACE>\fR
Destination namespace, for example acme/webapp
.TP
\fB\-\-as\fR \fI<IDENTITY>\fR
Act as this identity (`user:alice`, `agent:bot#run_…`, `service:ci`). Also: AG_IDENTITY
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Verify the migration and report limitations without publishing a repository
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-lossy\fR
Accept reported omissions, unresolved LFS pointers and unsupported refs
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Machine\-readable JSON output
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR
Colour the output: auto (a terminal, unless NO_COLOR is set), always or never
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print only what was asked for: no confirmations or hints. Errors and refusals are still shown
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Explain what is happening on standard error: repository, identity, remote, timing
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
<\fISOURCE\fR>
Full local Git clone, mirror or self\-contained .bundle file
.TP
<\fIDESTINATION\fR>
New destination directory. It must not exist
.SH VERSION
v0.3.0\-beta.2
